  "status": "verified-sample",
  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 6 actions (pjlink.js buildActions, line 700; the callbacks are attached in a loop at line 765) and 7 boolean feedbacks (init_feedbacks, line 1145). The actions and feedbacks are rebuilt (updateDynamicContent) when the projector reports its input list, so the input dropdowns change at runtime.",
    "PJLink over TCP, port config.port or 4352 (pjlink.js:192; there is no port config field). Config fields (not in the schema): host, password (empty for none), pollTime in seconds (default 5), debug. The module's idle-disconnect logic follows the PJLink rule of closing the connection after 30 seconds without pending commands (comment at pjlink.js:586).",
    "All dropdown ids are strings ('0', '1', '2', '3'), built by ar2obj (index as string) from the arrays in choices.js: ON_OFF_TOGGLE Off/On/Toggle, MUTE_ITEM Not Muted/Video Mute/Audio Mute/A/V Mute, ON_OFF_STATE Off/On, ERROR_STATE No Error/Warning/Error, POWER_STATE Off/On/Cooling/Warm-up. Error type ids are the strings errorFan, errorLamp, errorTemp, errorCover, errorFilter, errorOther.",
    "Quirk in the source: the mute action's 'Select Mute' default is '3' (A/V Mute) and its 'Select State' default is '0' (Off); the mute feedback defaults are item '3', state '1'. The feedback 'powerState' uses ids '0'-'3' where '2' is Cooling and '3' Warm-up.",
    "The class 2 commands (freeze, volume) are sent as %2... and only work with Class 2 projectors, as the action names say.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ^1.11.3: options do not support expressions."
  ],
  "actions": [
    {
      "id": "powerState",
      "name": "Change Projector Power State",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "opt",
          "type": "dropdown",
          "label": "Select Power State",
          "default": "1",
          "choices": [
